  "2026-11-12T11:56:13.896Z",codex-agent,"Read full PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs62gwZe including its AI-agent prompt; finding is valid. Main remains at 35fa518 and is already merged; worktree was clean at 29f5e26. generationProvenance excludes policy_evaluation, so birth-time refusal can drift undetected. Preserve the complete birth policy_evaluation via the shared verifySealedBirth check on every causal consumer. Intended post-birth addition: recordRefusedPolicyCard -> sealPolicyRejection -> validateRefusedPolicyCard attaches {decision: refuse, reason_digest: hashJson(reason)} (and captured evaluation_evidence when available) to a Generation whose verdict was absent. Plan real SDK body-update, native CLI-update, replay and checkpoint-publication refusal cases, plus idempotent and real post-birth rejection controls. Every refusal gets an isolated function-only revert proof. Local gates are affected importing test files, lint, typecheck and generated changelog check; full CI gate remains assigned to CI."
  "2026-11-12T12:04:05.905Z",codex-agent,"The focused real-SDK run passed its initial 11 cases, including preserved refusal, idempotent rewrite and actual post-birth recordRefusedPolicyCard addition/retry. Split SDK and CLI replay into independent regressions. The first proof batch correctly rejected the CLI case's unrelated missing-checkpoint diagnostic rather than accepting it as proof; strengthened both replay fixtures to own a valid checkpoint before changing a frozen birth reason. Re-running all ten refusals independently against the single verifySealedBirth guard, retaining measured diagnostic admission and restoration. Existing native-envelope checks still run before Generation parsing."
  "2026-11-12T12:07:02.770Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs62gwZe behavioral proof complete: all 10 independently selected refusal regressions produce exactly 0 pass / 1 fail with ERR_ASSERTION and Missing expected rejection after removing only verifySealedBirth's birth-verdict comparison; each restored implementation produces 1 pass / 0 fail. Cases: SDK decision, reason, nested value, added key, removed key, missing verdict, null verdict; checkpoint publication after refuse-to-promote; CLI body mutation followed independently by SDK and CLI replay of an owned checkpoint. Used node test/evaluation-lifecycle.revert.ts with the ten exact selectors recorded in docs/evaluation-lifecycle-birth-verdict-revert.json, inside a disposable source copy with a 1200-second cap; reviewed source was never mutated. The old multi-feature proof receipt remains untouched. Running the importing lifecycle files and the proof-generator consumer together next, retaining 100% lifecycle coverage thresholds."
  "2026-11-12T12:15:49.353Z",codex-agent,"Final runtime gate passed via timeout --kill-after=10s 1200s node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-rl-lifecycle --run --only-last --progress: 36/36 tests across both direct evaluation-lifecycle importers and the proof-generator consumer, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 100% evaluation-lifecycle.ts lines/branches/functions, 293.2 seconds. All 10 independent refusal mutants fail with the expected assertion and all restorations pass. The intended real post-birth refusal addition, reordered-key idempotent rewrite, preflight and registration retries pass. Supplemental npm run build:test caught fixture-only typing, now corrected to GenerationRegistrationRequest evaluation type; corrected fixture emits byte-identical JavaScript to the passing runtime gate and build:test passes. Final npm run lint and npm run typecheck pass, each capped at 1200 seconds. Also ran node test/evaluation-lifecycle.acceptance.ts public-source/.agents/pm 35fa51816d0fb998b14891541281911105d9a3bc in a disposable source copy populated with git archive origin/main .agents/pm: 64 public records replayed on a non-Git target, source unchanged, statistical verdict refuse. No retained public replay receipt overwritten. Remaining local gate is changelog generation/check; full release gate belongs to CI. No new CLI/SDK defects or open implementation blockers."
  "2026-11-12T12:16:08.905Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs62gwZe is addressed by preserving the entire birth-time policy_evaluation in verifySealedBirth; all ten tamper refusals fail independently on revert and both must-allow paths pass. Changelog regeneration and changelog:check also passed within the command cap. Final tracker writes and claim release are followed by fresh generation/check before commit and push. The thread was not answered, resolved or reacted to. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification; CI certifies the full gate."
  "2026-11-12T14:37:02.563Z",steve-orchestrator,"Orchestrator, CodeRabbit round on 4769607 (5 minor findings), fixed directly. (1) PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs62ncF1: the shared refusal matcher also requires EXIT_CODE.CONFLICT; a matcher test fails on revert. (2) PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs62ncF3: one shared isolatedChildEnv (test/fixtures/child-env.ts) removes every credential-named variable, including API, access and private keys, auth material and cookies, while keeping PM_AUTHOR; it is used by the proof runner and the CLI replay test, and a real proof child asserts OPENAI_API_KEY is absent (fails on revert). (3) PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs62ncF-: trackerDigest length-prefixes each path and body; the a.json='b.json' versus a.json+b.json collision now differs (fails on revert). (4) PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs62ncFu: the acceptance verifies the named commit by digesting that commit's .agents/pm via git archive and refusing on mismatch; tests cover the right commit, another real commit, an edited copy and a short SHA (fails on revert). The receipt was regenerated with the documented command against 701aaca: only authoritative_digest changed, as expected from the framing. (5) Outside-diff verdict-test:82: the CLI replay launches the pm entry from the package manifest with process.execPath instead of the extensionless .bin shim; CI is Linux-only, so this one cannot fail on revert there. Gates: replay-order + proof 11/11, lifecycle + verdict 30/30, lint, typecheck, docstring, changelog:check."
  "2026-11-12T19:46:37.547Z",steve-orchestrator,"Orchestrator fixes for CodeRabbit review of a788e50: (1) test/fixtures/child-env.ts filters every AUTH-bearing name; only exact authorship names (PM_AUTHOR, GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL/DATE) pass. The previous AUTH(?!OR) exception let HTTP_AUTHORIZATION-style names reach child processes. The proof test now also refuses HTTP_AUTHORIZATION, GITHUB_AUTHORIZATION, PM_AUTHORIZATION and PM_AUTHOR_TOKEN and still passes PM_AUTHOR and GIT_AUTHOR_* (fails on revert). (2) The conflict-exit refusal matcher moved to test/fixtures/refused.ts; the verdict test's drift matcher uses it, so it requires EXIT_CODE.CONFLICT as well as eval_plan_drift. (3) Probing showed new-candidate registration after collection drift always refuses with card_drift at the policy card, never reaching causal validation, so the eval_plan_drift-or-card_drift assertion hid that. It now pins card_drift, and a new test registers the candidate first and shows the registration retry refuses with eval_plan_drift in verifyCausalEvaluationRetry (preflight and write), with history and items unchanged, then admits the retry once the birth collection is restored. Disabling the causal retry check fails the new test. Gate: evaluation-lifecycle, -verdict, -proof tests (39 pass), tsc, lint, duplicates (0 clones)."
  "2026-11-12T21:04:54.234Z",codex-agent,"Read full PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs620MlG and PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs620MlK including both AI-agent prompts. Worktree clean at 5945566; main unchanged at 35fa518 and already merged. Extend causal verdict integrity from birth-only comparison to write-once native history: first stored policy_evaluation seals all later snapshots and live state, including removal and restored-current attempts; histories use verified durable revision coordinates, never clocks or sidecars. All causal readers, appendSequentialLook and retries already share the validator; preserve that single boundary and reuse native birth reads. IPC waiter must reject any child exit before its requested state, including code 0. Plan real SDK/CLI tamper and no-write publication tests plus first-addition/idempotent/no-verdict controls; bounded real-child clean-exit regression; isolated function-only revert evidence. Run importing files, lint, typecheck and generated changelog check with 1200-second caps; CI owns full certification."
  "2026-11-12T21:11:11.151Z",codex-agent,"Focused SDK gate passed 17/17 write-once cases; focused IPC clean-exit regression passed 1/1. Must-refuse matrix covers SDK promote, CLI promote and verdict removal through validation, SDK replay, CLI replay and append; each checks unchanged native history and absent next checkpoint. Additional cases cover changing a reason, restoring current state after historical tamper, and direct native retry verification. Must-allow cases cover actual first recordRefusedPolicyCard addition, equal reordered verdict rewrites, registration retries and candidates that never acquire a verdict. Native birth snapshots are reused; only Generation histories are scanned, with unbounded verified SDK compact history ordered by durable revision. The IPC helper uses the existing complete child-environment sanitizer. Running all 16 isolated function-only failure/restoration pairs now; no previous receipts rewritten."
  "2026-11-12T21:20:13.426Z",codex-agent,"Both round regressions proved independently: 15 write-once refusal cases and the IPC clean-exit case each fail with one measured ERR_ASSERTION under a function-only revert and pass after restoration. Write-once failures are Missing expected rejection; IPC failure is Clean worker exit must reject committed, after the real worker exits 0 and the old waiter remains pending. No timeout or process-status failure was accepted as proof. Receipt docs/evaluation-lifecycle-write-once-revert.json records all 16 selected pairs, base commit 5945566 and hashes of tested source files; source bytes stayed unchanged. Histories and previous proof receipts remain intact. Running all direct importing lifecycle test files plus the proof-generator consumer together now, at unchanged 100% module lines/branches/functions thresholds."
  "2026-11-12T21:27:34.754Z",codex-agent,"Final affected-file gate passed: timeout --kill-after=10s 1200s node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-rl-lifecycle --run --only-last --progress executed evaluation-lifecycle.test.ts, evaluation-lifecycle-verdict.test.ts and evaluation-lifecycle-proof.test.ts: 57/57, zero failures/skips/cancellations, evaluation-lifecycle.ts 100% lines/branches/functions, 291.8 seconds. All 16 isolated function-only revert/restoration pairs pass; source-bound receipt hashes match final source. Required SDK/CLI promote and deletion cases refuse through validation, both replay paths and appendSequentialLook, without history or checkpoint writes; first addition, equal rewrite and no-verdict candidates pass. Native retry and historical-tamper restoration cases also pass. The real code-0 IPC worker is rejected before committed; reverting only that handler leaves the promise pending and fails the bounded assertion. Public lifecycle acceptance also passed using a verified git archive of main 35fa518: 64 records, source unchanged, non-Git target, descriptive verdict refuse. Final npm run lint, npm run typecheck and npm run build:test passed with individual 1200-second caps. No previous receipts or native history records rewritten. Changelog generation/check is the remaining local gate; full release certification remains assigned to CI. No new SDK/CLI defect or implementation blocker established."
  "2026-11-12T21:28:29.270Z",codex-agent,"Both PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs620MlG and PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs620MlK are addressed; changelog:full and changelog:check also passed within their caps. Final tracker writes and claim release are followed by fresh changelog generation/check before commit and normal push. Verdict integrity is shared across causal reads, checkpoint publication and retries; verified native item history supplies the first verdict and every later state is checked. The IPC waiter rejects every premature exit while successful IPC resolution remains intact. No review replies, resolutions or reactions were made. Item stays in progress for orchestrator verification; full CI certification remains outside this local gate budget."
  "2026-11-12T21:52:46.641Z",orchestrator,"Orchestrator, CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs622OWb and PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs622OWp on b879510. (1) The docs/evaluation-lifecycle.md command block now uses the linked example plan's candidate rl-sequential-candidate (the incumbent rl-seed already matched). (2) The receipt subprocess in test/evaluation-lifecycle-proof.test.ts uses the shared isolatedChildEnv() filter instead of a local regex that kept OPENAI_API_KEY and HTTP_AUTHORIZATION. Gate: evaluation-lifecycle-proof passes 8/8 with OPENAI_API_KEY set in the parent; lint and typecheck pass."
  "2026-11-12T23:47:51.267Z",orchestrator,"Orchestrator, CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs624jzS and PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs624jzY on 599189e. (1) The OS-process replay test now exercises the lost acknowledgement. In the causal worker's kill-before-ack mode the worker SIGKILLs itself after causalStep's durable write and before sending committed. The parent asserts that the worker never acknowledged, that the history changed, and that the retry leaves the history bytes unchanged, for the candidate, first and last steps. (2) isolatedChildEnv filters PAT as a delimited word (GITHUB_PAT, PAT, PAT_GITHUB), while PATH_PREFIX and SPATIAL_MODE stay as must-allow. Revert proof: without the PAT term the credential test fails 1 of 1. Gates: evaluation-lifecycle and evaluation-lifecycle-proof pass 28/28; lint and typecheck pass."
